{
  "id": "m1l4",
  "title": {
    "es": "Funciones: def, parámetros y return",
    "en": "Functions: def, parameters and return"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "¿Qué es una función?"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Una **función** es un bloque de código con nombre que puedes reutilizar. Se define con `def`, recibe datos de entrada (parámetros) y puede devolver un resultado con `return`."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def saludar(nombre):",
          "    return 'Hola, ' + nombre",
          "",
          "print(saludar('Ana'))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "Hola, Ana"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Fíjate en la estructura: `def nombre(parametros):` y, debajo, el cuerpo **indentado** (sangrado con 4 espacios). La indentación es la que delimita qué pertenece a la función."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "return frente a print"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`print` solo *muestra* algo en pantalla; `return` *entrega* un valor a quien llamó a la función para poder seguir trabajando con él. Casi siempre querrás `return`."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def doble(n):",
          "    return n * 2",
          "",
          "resultado = doble(5)",
          "print(resultado + 1)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "11"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Cuando se ejecuta `return`, la función termina inmediatamente. Si una función no tiene `return`, devuelve `None` (nada)."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Varios parámetros y valores por defecto"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Una función puede recibir varios parámetros separados por comas, y puedes darles un valor por defecto que se usa si no se pasa ese argumento."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def potencia(base, exponente=2):",
          "    return base ** exponente",
          "",
          "print(potencia(3))",
          "print(potencia(2, 10))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "9",
          "1024"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Una función bien hecha hace **una sola cosa** y tiene un nombre que describe qué devuelve. Si te cuesta nombrarla, quizá hace demasiado."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "What is a function?"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "A **function** is a named block of code you can reuse. You define it with `def`, it receives input data (parameters) and can return a result with `return`."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def greet(name):",
          "    return 'Hello, ' + name",
          "",
          "print(greet('Ana'))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "Hello, Ana"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Notice the structure: `def name(parameters):` and, below, the **indented** body (4 spaces). Indentation is what defines what belongs to the function."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "return versus print"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`print` only *shows* something on screen; `return` *hands* a value back to the caller so you can keep working with it. You will almost always want `return`."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def double(n):",
          "    return n * 2",
          "",
          "result = double(5)",
          "print(result + 1)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "11"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "When `return` runs, the function ends immediately. If a function has no `return`, it returns `None` (nothing)."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Several parameters and default values"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "A function can take several comma-separated parameters, and you can give them a default value used when that argument is not passed."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def power(base, exponent=2):",
          "    return base ** exponent",
          "",
          "print(power(3))",
          "print(power(2, 10))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "9",
          "1024"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "A well-made function does **one thing** and has a name that describes what it returns. If it is hard to name, it may be doing too much."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m1l4e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define una función `doble(n)` que devuelva el doble de `n` (es decir, `n * 2`).",
        "en": "Define a function `doble(n)` that returns the double of `n` (that is, `n * 2`)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def doble(n):",
        "    # devuelve el doble de n",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def doble(n):",
        "    return n * 2"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Usa return, no print.",
          "return n * 2"
        ],
        "en": [
          "Use return, not print.",
          "return n * 2"
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "name": "doble",
          "function": "doble",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                5
              ],
              "expected": 10
            },
            {
              "args": [
                0
              ],
              "expected": 0
            },
            {
              "args": [
                -3
              ],
              "expected": -6
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m1l4e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `area_rectangulo(base, altura)` que devuelva el área del rectángulo (base por altura).",
        "en": "Define `area_rectangulo(base, altura)` that returns the rectangle area (base times height)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def area_rectangulo(base, altura):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def area_rectangulo(base, altura):",
        "    return base * altura"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "El área es base * altura."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Area is base * height."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "name": "area",
          "function": "area_rectangulo",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                2,
                3
              ],
              "expected": 6
            },
            {
              "args": [
                5,
                5
              ],
              "expected": 25
            },
            {
              "args": [
                10,
                0
              ],
              "expected": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m1l4e3",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `es_par(n)` que devuelva `True` si `n` es par y `False` si es impar. Pista: usa el operador módulo `%`.",
        "en": "Define `es_par(n)` that returns `True` if `n` is even and `False` if it is odd. Hint: use the modulo operator `%`."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def es_par(n):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def es_par(n):",
        "    return n % 2 == 0"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Un número es par si el resto de dividir entre 2 es 0.",
          "return n % 2 == 0"
        ],
        "en": [
          "A number is even if the remainder of dividing by 2 is 0.",
          "return n % 2 == 0"
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "name": "es_par",
          "function": "es_par",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                4
              ],
              "expected": true
            },
            {
              "args": [
                7
              ],
              "expected": false
            },
            {
              "args": [
                0
              ],
              "expected": true
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}